  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satish Sharma vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 28 September, 2020",
    "facts": "The applicant has filed this first bail application u/S.439 Cr.P.C for grant of bail. Applicant has been arrested on 21.02.2020 by Police Station Jaura, District Morena, in connection with Crime No.504/2019 registered for offence under Sections 420, 272 and 273 of IPC and 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act. It is the submission of counsel for the applicant that applicant is suffering confinement since 21.02.2020 on false pretext and was instrumental alongwith main accused Gyani Sharma regarding offences referred above. It is further submitted that prime accused Gyani Sharma who faced wrath of prosecution and provisions of National Security Act were imposed over him and he was instrumental in doing all the things. Applicant is relative of Gyani Sharma and on the basis of statement of Gyani Sharma wherein role of applicant has been referred therefore, applicant was implicated and confined. Under these grounds, he prayed for grant of bail to the applicant. Counsel for the State opposed the prayer and prayed for dismissal of application.",
    "arguments": "Looking to the nature of allegation, applicant seeks bail on the ground that he is innocent and even otherwise, he lerant the lesson hard way and would mend his ways and become a better citizen. He would not involve in any such criminal activity in future. He felt trappings of health hazardous to the common public. He undertakes to perform community service. He undertakes to cooperate in the trial as well as in the investigation as and when required.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Looking to the nature of allegation, applicant seeks bail on the ground that he is innocent and even otherwise, he lerant the lesson hard way and would mend his ways and become a better citizen. He would not involve in any such criminal activity in future. He felt trappings of health hazardous to the common public. He undertakes to perform community service. He undertakes to cooperate in the trial as well as in the investigation as and when required.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
